      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "2010 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The diastereoselective synthesis of (+/-)-trans-4-hydroxy-6-propyl-1-oxocyclohexan-2-one, as a mixture trans:cis (3:1), was accomplished using a protocol that combine the Prins cyclization and RuO(4) oxidation. The synthesis this lactone allowed the elucidation of the correct structure of the substance isolated from the barks of Vitex cymosa. The delta-lactones mixture showed significant antinociceptive properties in preliminary tests using the tail flick model assay."
      },
